        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: exīstimō, exīstimāre",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "exīstimō, exīstimāre — \"to reckon, to consider; to value\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Quid dē hōc librō exīstimās? What do you think of this book?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "exīstimō, exīstimāre, exīstimāvī, exīstimātum. With the accusative and infinitive: exīstimō tē errāre, I reckon you are wrong."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "exīstimō is built from ex \"out\" and aestimō \"to value, to put a price on\" (Lewis & Short): to weigh a thing up and give the result. English estimate and esteem come from aestimō."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
